# Split-horizon resolver for out-of-band (blind) vulnerability confirmation: a
# blind vuln only proves itself by making the target call out to the interactsh
# sink, so the target must resolve *.interactsh.local there without losing its
# ordinary lookups. → DECISIONS.md.
#
# - interactsh.local (+ subdomains) forwards to interactsh's own DNS
#   (172.19.0.250:53), which records the interaction and answers with the sink IP.
# - Everything else forwards to Docker's embedded DNS (127.0.0.11), so the target
#   still resolves its DB, sibling services and external names.
# - Only the scanned OOB target points its `dns:` here; nuclei is pointed at the
#   same resolver (--dns) so its callback host is one this resolver answers.

interactsh.local {
    forward . 172.19.0.250:53
}

. {
    forward . 127.0.0.11
    cache 30
}
